# EmailJS Browser Configuration (Client-side safe public keys)
# 1. Sign up for free at https://www.emailjs.com/
# 2. Add an Email Service (e.g. Gmail) -> get Service ID
# 3. Create an Email Template -> get Template ID
# 4. Under Account > Public Key -> get Public Key
#
# Create a local .env file in the project root and fill in your actual values:
VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=your_service_id
VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=your_template_id
VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=your_public_key
